data.content:
Output matches the expected format. Here's the key part:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Jane", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase };
Console.WriteLine(JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options));

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

`JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` converts `Name` → `name` and `Age` → `age`. No extra NuGet packages needed — `System.Text.Json` is built into .NET 8.
